  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.44 Mold-seal coating",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.44 “Mold-seal coating” means the initial coating applied to a new mold or a repaired mold to provide a smooth surface which, when coated with a mold release coating, prevents products from sticking to the mold.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
